#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "842161b7-0cab-5ebd-a4ed-0ffcd0c29574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi^2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "842161b7-0cab-5ebd-a4ed-0ffcd0c29574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi^2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309040} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea492ab3-cc2a-5743-9b68-03b6b0b54dc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "af9f658c-f88f-52fc-86e4-26004d3557fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-348852" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }[6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})=3(1-cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,\\,[6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]dx & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,\\,[3-3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
